    "empirical_contention_diagnosis": "The uncontended critical section is fast (median hold 2.99-3.5 ms). However, under multi-process contention on Windows, when Process A holds the msvcrt file lock, competing processes encounter PermissionError [Errno 13] and enter an exponential backoff loop (store.py:388-412: sleep_s starts at 2ms and grows by 1.4x up to 50ms). Because competing processes are put to sleep, when Process A releases the lock at ~3ms, all other processes are asleep, leaving the lock idle for 10-40ms before the next process wakes up. This sleep-induced convoy effect accounts for >80% of elapsed time under 10 processes.",
    "architectural_remediation_proposal": "Concrete Remediation Plan (Scheduled for Future Release, Zero Code Changes to Current Branch):\n1. Granular Lock Scope: Move the read-only vector deduplication query outside namespace_write_lock,    scoping the advisory lock strictly to the atomic SQLite insert/update.\n2. SQLite Native Concurrency: Set PRAGMA busy_timeout = 5000 in WAL mode to delegate lock scheduling    to SQLite's internal page-level mutexes rather than gross file locks.\n3. Randomized Microsecond Jitter: Replace coarse exponential backoff (2-50ms) with randomized microsecond    jitter (200us - 1.5ms) to eliminate convoy formation."
